course: dictionary
lesson: 9739
title: Sunset: a time and a sight
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sunset is a word with two meanings. The first is a time: the evening moment when the sun goes down below the horizon. «The stones of Stonehenge line up with the sunrise in midsummer and the sunset in midwinter.» Here sunset is a time of day.
explain: The second meaning is a sight: the colours in the sky as the sun goes down. «Watch the sunset» means look at the sky while it turns orange, pink or red. The words around the word give the clue: «at sunset» usually means a time, while «watch the sunset» usually means the colours.
explain: Sunset can also mean an ending. «Ride off into the sunset» is a phrase from stories, and it means the story is finishing. Ask yourself what would fit, then check your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Sunset is the time in the evening when the sun goes below the horizon.
fact: A sunset is also the colours in the sky when the sun goes down.
fact: The Earth spins, so the sun seems to set in the west each evening.
fact: Sunset times change with the seasons: later in summer and earlier in winter.
exercise: «The stones of Stonehenge line up with the sunrise in midsummer and the sunset in midwinter.» In this sentence, what is sunset? | A kind of stone | *A time, when the sun goes below the horizon | A summer holiday | A colour of the sky only
exercise: «Ride off into the sunset» is a phrase from stories. What does sunset mean in this phrase? | A type of horse | *The end, as at the end of a story | A sunrise in the morning | A long walk home
exercise: Sunset times change with the seasons. In which season is sunset earliest? | *Winter | Spring | Autumn | Summer
test: «Mercury is seen only low in the sky just after sunset.» What does sunset mean here? | A sunrise in the morning | *A time, just after the sun goes below the horizon | A colour in a painting | The Moon rising in the night
test: Why does the Sun look yellowish, and red at sunset? | The Sun turns red each evening | *Our air scatters blue light | Clouds paint the Sun | The Sun is closer to Earth at sunset
exam: Which sentence uses sunset to mean the colours in the sky? | Mercury is hard to spot, so look low in the sky | Ramadan starts about 11 days earlier each year | *Watch the sunset and see the orange and pink clouds | Stonehenge lines up with the sunrise in midsummer
